// serve, the static file server at the repository's top (serve/PLAN.md), built by its build
// program and run against Python's http.client and raw sockets, from
// tests/helpers/serve_peer.py, which serves a temporary directory and sends Ctrl-Break as
// tests/helpers/console_break.py does. Its own tests (`ctxc test serve`: targets resolved and
// refused, log lines, dates, content types) run first.
//
// Fetched: a file, and its HEAD; 3 MiB sent in chunks, the same bytes; a listing, its links
// percent-encoded and its names escaped as HTML; a directory without its `/` redirected, and
// its index.html; a name with a space and `&`; an empty directory's listing; a content type by
// extension; 404; `..` above the root, spelled plainly, percent-encoded and from below,
// refused with 403; a `\`, which Windows would read as a separator, and a device name, 404;
// POST, 405 with Allow; a head with a broken field, which serve_connection answers 400 and the
// connection's task logs; and /stats, counted across connections. Each request's access log
// line is read before the next request is sent, so the log is in order here.
//
// Stopping: after a Ctrl-Break the server stops accepting; a kept-alive connection's request is
// answered with Connection: close, and an idle one is cancelled at the end of the 2-second
// grace period; it exits with 0. A server of one connection at most (--connections 1) closes
// a second at once, and counts it refused; a second Ctrl-Break during its 60-second grace
// period ends it at once, as std's stop does.
